{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/167467-entering-dreams-and-the-pledge-of-horn-and-bone","id":167467,"title":"Entering dreams and the Pledge of Horn and Bone.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-12T20:23:53-07:00","id":167467,"title":"Entering dreams and the Pledge of Horn and Bone.","content":"Hello all,<br /> <br /> I'll be joining a Changeling game within a few weeks, and in reading through the system, I've found myself a bit stymied by oneiromancy. Most of it is fairly clear, what I'm not quite certain of is the start, that is, how you actually enter dreams, and the relation to that and the Pledge of Horn and Bone. I'm only referring to &quot;basic&quot; oneiromancy here, not Contracts of Dream or Skeinwalking.<br /> <br /> If I'm understanding what I've read correctly, other than personal and fetch dreams, in order for a Changeling to enter someone else's dreams they have to be pledged to the Changeling. Once pledged, the Changeling can spend a point of Glamour, make the extended meditation roll, and enter the mortal's dream, which allows them to shape it, harvest Glamour, etc. Assuming that they then safeguard the pledged person's dream, when they exit, they receive an additional point of Glamour, effectively negating the original expenditure even if they didn't make any Harvest rolls.<br /> <br /> Am I on the right track here, or did I miss something? It just seems unnecessarily complicated for what's effectively a net zero expenditure endeavor. I also want to make sure I understand the relation of Horn and Bone to oneiromancy correctly.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for clarification, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3283-wussydan","name":"WussyDan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T20:36:46-07:00","id":167503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WussyDan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/167467-entering-dreams-and-the-pledge-of-horn-and-bone#post167467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I on the right track here, or did I miss something? It just seems unnecessarily complicated for what's effectively a net zero expenditure endeavor. I also want to make sure I understand the relation of Horn and Bone to oneiromancy correctly.</div> </div> </div> </div>The part where you assume this is unnecessarily complicated breaks down when considering that the Pledge of Horn and Bone is not the sole variety of pledgecraft that can contain the Dreaming task.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T22:57:15-07:00","id":167597,"title":"","content":"Read the sections Dreamriding and Dreamscaping starting on p 194. There's more to do in dreams than just harvest glamour. You can do all sorts of nifty things to help the mortal (or in some cases<i> your</i> future interactions with that mortal). Learn about the target, heal them, teach them things (reducing xp costs), etc. Dream stuff is really cool and should never be ignored in a Changeling game. Just think of that Pledge as your &quot;ticket&quot; allowing entry.<br /> <br /> And don't forget you have to be in the Hedge (at least within a Hollow) to enter another's dreams.<br /> <br /> And Satchel's right, you could craft a Pledge that includes the dreaming task and is <i>vastly </i>different than the Horn and Bone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2523-tiarn","name":"Tiarn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T08:51:35-07:00","id":167953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiarn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/167467-entering-dreams-and-the-pledge-of-horn-and-bone?p=167597#post167597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just think of that Pledge as your &quot;ticket&quot; allowing entry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, that was really what I wanted to double check. Whether it's Horn and Bone or not, in order to enter a mortal's dreams (barring tokens/Contracts) they have to be pledged to the Changeling via a pledge that involves the Dreaming task.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3283-wussydan","name":"WussyDan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T21:58:31-07:00","id":170399,"title":"","content":"This is true.<br /> <br /> You can craft a dream to give to a mortal through the Contract of Dreams clause 2, but you can't actually enter in with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}